{"connection_id": "BC-c24c19474ea46e216d24", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.3.13", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "fire reveals quality of each work", "note": "Paul says the day exposes each person's work as fire tests its quality; it links the commentary's burning at the end to an evaluation of accumulated human work."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7b35a4026a94c3278a77", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.3.15", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "work burned and its maker suffers loss, yet is saved", "note": "The commentary likens failed works to ash blown away; Paul says a person's work may be burned and suffer loss while the person is saved, distinguishing lost product from lost person."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cd356cd3798d68d48591", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.3.15", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "work burns and worker loses", "note": "If a person's work burns, that person suffers loss even though saved; the precise distinction between a life and its ruined product clarifies the commentary's garden consumed late in life."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9ebdb7b1face425991f3", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.3.6", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "one plants, another waters, God gives growth", "note": "The commentary turns plants joined together into people who urge one another; Paul describes distinct workers planting and watering within one field, while God supplies the growth."}
{"connection_id": "BC-356cb01e3a1ff7ec7b7d", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.3.6", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "planting and watering; growth from God", "note": "Paul assigns planting and watering to different workers while God causes growth; the commentary's rain-fed community of mutually contributing lives receives a concrete division of work."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0b4db61d0a247c7b4ad2", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.9.10", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "plowman and thresher hope to share the crop", "note": "The commentary says produce has a due and pasture nourishes animals; Paul interprets the crop law as giving field workers hope of sharing the harvest, making labor and entitlement explicit."}
{"connection_id": "BC-48667aa0f31596bcb0db", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.1.24", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "flesh like grass; flower falls", "note": "The letter quotes human flesh as grass whose flower falls; it transposes the commentary's withering harvest to the brevity of human life."}
{"connection_id": "BC-847d4c5f5ad8dcadd45d", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Thess.5.14", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "admonish, encourage, help, and be patient with all", "note": "The commentary's exception consists of people who urge one another to truth and patience; Paul specifies communal admonition, encouragement of the fainthearted, help for the weak, and patience toward all."}
{"connection_id": "BC-59dcef698f46f964983d", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Thess.5.14", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "mutual counsel and patience with the weak", "note": "Paul directs the community to admonish some, encourage the fainthearted, help the weak, and be patient with everyone; this spells out the mutual exhortation and care for vulnerable members pictured by the commentary's connected plants."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cbf7522217be02a45e58", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.8.14", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "surplus answers another's lack", "note": "Paul asks that one community's present abundance supply another's need; this makes the commentary's mutually joined believers and harvest due a concrete exchange of resources."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f35768345f82388e1ed3", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.9.10", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "seed for sowing and a growing harvest of righteousness", "note": "The commentary joins good works to a crop image; Paul says God supplies seed and increases the harvest of righteousness, explicitly making ethical fruit the result."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ffd1b9a3586b216b5bba", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.9.10", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "seed and bread; harvest of righteousness", "note": "God supplies seed and food and multiplies the harvest of righteousness for givers; the commentary's rain-fed grain and obligation to share meet in this single farming image."}
{"connection_id": "BC-34be5db2408b36eac5b6", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.9.6", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "generous sowing yields a generous harvest", "note": "The commentary links righteous deeds and harvest; Paul applies sowing and reaping to generosity, making shared giving the deed that determines the yield."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0eb655879648cfe255c6", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.9.6", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "sowing generosity; proportional harvest", "note": "Paul's giving appeal says sparing and generous sowing have corresponding harvests; this adds the commentary's almsgiving setting to its agricultural account of human gain."}
{"connection_id": "BC-76718170813750aaaa3a", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.9.9", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "distribution to poor as righteousness", "note": "In Paul's quotation, one who distributes to the poor has righteousness that endures; it explains how the commentary's crop right at harvest becomes a lasting moral yield."}
{"connection_id": "BC-35eac61611a246aefcc0", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.15", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "truth spoken as the body grows", "note": "The commentary's people mutually counsel one another to truth; Ephesians joins speaking truth with growing into Christ, adding growth as the outcome of truthful communal practice."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5d43fadce6d97d967b46", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.15", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "truth spoken in love as growth", "note": "Speaking truth in love, believers grow toward Christ; this joins the commentary's charge to exhort in truth with its unusual image of shared living growth."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f6b5e2497f94ea418923", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.16", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "joined body grows as each part works", "note": "The commentary makes mutual counsel into plants connected as one green pasture; Ephesians describes a body joined together with every part working so it grows and builds itself up, a specific social counterpart to interconnected growth."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6274f91b010c120836ba", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.16", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "joined parts cause communal growth", "note": "The whole body is joined and held together, each part working so it grows in love; though anatomical rather than botanical, it develops the commentary's claim that the faithful sustain one another by being connected."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5f9a61f2cc8682d35411", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.10", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "do good especially to fellow believers", "note": "Immediately after the promised harvest for persistent good work, Paul directs good to all, especially the household of faith; it identifies the mutual beneficiaries of the commentary's patient moral crop."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3e6e45230351b571d937", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.7", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "what is sown is reaped", "note": "Paul says a person reaps what he sows; the commentary's crop as the product of a life receives an explicit ethical harvest formula."}
{"connection_id": "BC-61026d2b88c9aefaa213", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.8", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "sowing to flesh reaps corruption; sowing to Spirit reaps life", "note": "The commentary says humanity is in loss except those who do good; Paul assigns contrasting harvests to two ways of life, making the ethical distinction a direct sowing-and-reaping contrast."}
{"connection_id": "BC-36c294a9141b04353d85", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.8", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "corrupt or enduring harvest", "note": "Sowing to the flesh yields corruption while sowing to the Spirit yields life; the two outcomes sharpen the commentary's distinction between a ruined yield and enduring good action."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c2a6d0a1e86d0df55c1d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.9", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "doing good reaped in due season", "note": "The commentary links righteous action and patience; Paul says not to tire of doing good because the harvest comes at its season if they do not give up, making the ethical crop analogy explicit."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5095b64085aafa622f25", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.9", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "persist in good; harvest in time", "note": "Paul urges against growing weary in doing good because a harvest will come if one does not give up; it ties the commentary's patient mutual goodness to sustained crop growth."}

{"connection_id": "BC-dfd7ff0a9a3ba4acf479", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.24", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "consider one another for good works", "note": "The community is to attend to one another so as to stir love and good works; this gives a specific ethical action beside the commentary's joined plants representing believers who mutually urge what is right."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cdc15e418fa807166f43", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.3.13", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "exhort one another each day before hardening", "note": "The addressees must encourage one another daily while it is called Today so no one hardens; the commentary's reciprocal exhortation and closing time horizon meet in a concrete repeated practice."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3a77f894e4b00ff118df", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.6.7", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "rained land produces useful vegetation", "note": "The commentary's cloud gives rain and the exception is a green, productive community; Hebrews compares hearers to land that drinks frequent rain and produces useful vegetation, interpreting response as fruitful growth."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b6dd2e49f3e90110676a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.6.7", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "rain drunk by earth; useful crop", "note": "The earth repeatedly drinks rain and grows useful vegetation for its cultivators; this matches the commentary's rain-to-productive-growth sequence and makes the crop's value depend on what it yields."}
